   <property name="text">
    <string>&lt;html&gt;&lt;head/&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;p&gt;Here is the maturing stage where the beer is aged in order to develop a full flavor profile. Any remaining yeast or sediment will also settle to the bottom during this time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;An optional technique that can be applied at this time is dry hopping. Dry-hopping is the process of adding hops to the beer during the maturation stage, which can enhance the beer's flavor and aroma without contributing to any bitterness.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string>
